{"title":"1990 IMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Problems of the 1990 <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"IMO\">IMO</a>.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Day_I\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day I</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Day_II\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day II</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_I\">Day I</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Day I\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Chords <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> of a circle intersect at a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> inside the circle. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> be an interior point of the segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/b/4bbe91133fdaa92f3e58b137fdb4db178296da61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EB$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />. The tangent line at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to the circle through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> intersects the lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, respectively. If\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/9/31912eb26c7d2c8eea36251e6f29ccbd9824960e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac {AM}{AB} = t,\\]\" width=\"70\" height=\"37\" />\nfind <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/8/948b4271a10f0ac7ed7643d362405d95bf0d23ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {EG}{EF}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"31\" height=\"37\" /> in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1990 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/e/49e6a2d706867d6652d7edadccc3fd034130bd98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> and consider a set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/f/03f5a5ded7724c11e58ef212dc3e8549071890a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"50\" height=\"12\" /> distinct points on a circle. Suppose that exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> of these points are to be colored black. Such a coloring is good if there is at least one pair of black points such that the interior of one of the arcs between them contains exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> points from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Find the smallest value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> so that every such coloring of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> points of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is good.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1990 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Determine all integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/d/49d98ffe996c0f0d3b82b284cba2113439fefea9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" /> such that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/b/c5b07c4edac28bfd646e5ba3bbd8a92cb15655ac.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac {2^n + 1}{n^2}\\]\" width=\"49\" height=\"37\" /> is an integer.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1990 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_II\">Day II</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Day II\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/0/f70493b87d0fb79a8e9fb7958757dd229c13f6c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\mathbb Q}^ +$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"23\" height=\"18\" /> be the set of positive rational numbers. Construct a function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/5/475221665f3aa8d7a8ea9c4ae3aa48e81830f2e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f : {\\mathbb Q}^ + \\rightarrow {\\mathbb Q}^ +$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"102\" height=\"18\" /> such that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/4/0c4f167b3298fb2610322ecf667658bc2455a059.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(xf(y)) = \\frac {f(x)}{y}\\]\" width=\"131\" height=\"42\" />\nfor all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/0/f70493b87d0fb79a8e9fb7958757dd229c13f6c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\mathbb Q}^ +$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"23\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1990 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Given an initial integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/d/5cd12d1f8d2c5878e54c1900f926d1fd3d635d1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_0 &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" />, two players, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/d/c3dee18eeb2fe8f2004b2cd11f90c8d1b15c594f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\mathcal A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/c/2bcfbd586573c22bde860a37136ebd2747e0cc7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\mathcal B}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" />, choose integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/f/defbf06b987965438e5928b96688e48df84cba0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/c/85c5df946080fc6ec1ee0a560a8e8c5e6699113c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/c/baca093ae46e7ff420aa90bfeed14840391a65a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/5/3958e984d2597b35da7975f4503cdcf965a777f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ldots$\" width=\"19\" height=\"2\" /> alternately according to the following rules&#160;:\n</p><p>I.) Knowing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/3/e9328c603179810edee02ab90a633bebbfdacd5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_{2k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"24\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/7/0b7bf42db84e4d2dbb7bf55476c12bf9f6233bc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> chooses any integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/4/5240bf913622eec03b518fbc5971ff9c22a36231.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_{2k + 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" /> such that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/d/6fd67fb9c74abb101bc435b3aa429cee48e6aecb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n_{2k} \\leq n_{2k + 1} \\leq n_{2k}^2.\\]\" width=\"145\" height=\"20\" /> \n</p><p>II.) Knowing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/4/5240bf913622eec03b518fbc5971ff9c22a36231.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_{2k + 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/c/2bcfbd586573c22bde860a37136ebd2747e0cc7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\mathcal B}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> chooses any integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/0/1603799c36a6045cba99cd3e915dd2e5aa25a05a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_{2k + 2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f9699ba4b6b65b2eb207ae39c67b96a030dc18d2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{n_{2k + 1}}{n_{2k + 2}}\\]\" width=\"43\" height=\"37\" /> \nis a prime raised to a positive integer power.\n</p><p>Player <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/d/c3dee18eeb2fe8f2004b2cd11f90c8d1b15c594f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\mathcal A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> wins the game by choosing the number 1990; player <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/c/2bcfbd586573c22bde860a37136ebd2747e0cc7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\mathcal B}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> wins by choosing the number 1. For which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/f/b2f0c6d216bb63a89845904c513ec0007b6b3e7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> does&#160;:\n</p><p><br />\na.) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/d/c3dee18eeb2fe8f2004b2cd11f90c8d1b15c594f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\mathcal A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> have a winning strategy?\nb.) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/c/2bcfbd586573c22bde860a37136ebd2747e0cc7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\mathcal B}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> have a winning strategy?\nc.) Neither player have a winning strategy?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1990 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Prove that there exists a convex 1990-gon with the following two properties&#160;:\n</p><p>a.) All angles are equal.\nb.) The lengths of the 1990 sides are the numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/1/c716d1dc907ae6b51cb0f545664c89d58b6b67d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/a/32a35631e1e126934ead6d2af161e9d250827bbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^2$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/9/819068968ed60608a91d0c3921d6296964660e9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/7/087594ea26fa196b8e61bc20a36228270dc695f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cdots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"26\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/8/e08b9f75fcf527daecab9dec9d3289e17d86d716.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1990^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> in some order.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1990 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_IMO\" title=\"1990 IMO\">1990 IMO</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=1&amp;cid=16&amp;year=1990\">IMO 1990 Problems on the Resources page</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions,_with_authors\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions, with authors\">IMO Problems and Solutions, with authors</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics_competition_resources\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Mathematics competition resources\">Mathematics competition resources</a></li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_IMO\" title=\"1990 IMO\">1990 IMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_IMO\" title=\"1989 IMO\">1989 IMO</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1990 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1990 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1990 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1990 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1990 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1990 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_IMO\" title=\"1991 IMO\">1991 IMO</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018043446\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.036 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.051 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 331/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 837/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 56/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 10120/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.525      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    6.525      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:20547:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018043446 and revision id 180322. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}